WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:05.200
Our heroes have now arrived in Fleurrh City,

2
00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:08.800
where Serena's next Pokémon Showcase is about to be held.

3
00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:13.433
One more Princess Key to go. I've got to win it here.

4
00:00:13.866 --> 00:00:19.133
- Go for it. Give it everything you've got.
- You'll do fine. Just be confident.

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.733
Clemont's right. We'll be cheering for you, too.

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.233
Pikachu!

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.233
Huh?

8
00:00:24.766 --> 00:00:27.166
Thanks. That means a lot to me.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.033
Huh?

10
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.866
- Wonder what's going on.
- So many people.

11
00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.633
Amelia, you'll win your third Princess Key!

12
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.666
We know it!

13
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:39.833
Can't wait to see you in Master Class.

14
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.900
Oh, my, somebody here will become Kalos Queen.

15
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:47.500
I guess that means she's going to enter the Pokémon Showcase, as well.

16
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.400
She sure looks popular.

17
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:53.700
Huh?

18
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:55.866
Oh.

19
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:09.333
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

20
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.266
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

21
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.166
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

22
00:01:17.233 --> 00:01:19.833
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

23
00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:21.533
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

24
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.733
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

25
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.966
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

26
00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.700
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

27
00:01:46.366 --> 00:01:47.533
Huh?

28
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:51.666
Uh, is something wrong with your stomach, Serena?

29
00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:54.066
Huh? Mm-mm.

30
00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.566
- I'm fine.
- You need to eat a lot of food

31
00:01:56.633 --> 00:02:00.433
before you compete, or you won't have enough strength.

32
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.300
You know Ash always eats a lot of food, right?

33
00:02:03.366 --> 00:02:05.366
- Gives him energy.
- You bet.

34
00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:06.733
Pika!

35
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.400
- That's our Ash, all right.
- Hmm.

36
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.366
Okay, I'm all set to go.

37
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:21.466
- Good luck, Serena.
- We'll be cheering for you bigtime.

38
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.733
Just stay confident.

39
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.333
- Braix.
- Cham.

40
00:02:26.466 --> 00:02:28.300
- Bunnelby.
- Yon.

41
00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:30.733
- Chespin, Che.
- Huh?

42
00:02:31.533 --> 00:02:32.500
Yon.

43
00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.033
Thank you. I'm sure we'll win.

44
00:02:43.166 --> 00:02:44.333
Here we go.

45
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.566
- Excuse me.
- Huh?

46
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.333
We're to be onstage right away.

47
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.933
Oh. Sorry.

48
00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.466
Huh? Oh.

49
00:03:09.966 --> 00:03:12.766
- I guess we'd better get ready, too.
- Braixen.

50
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.000
I've been waiting for you.

51
00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:20.066
Your attendance will make this Showcase livelier.

52
00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:23.600
- The performers make the Showcase lively.
- Yes, of course.

53
00:03:24.066 --> 00:03:27.000
There's a performer I'd like to introduce to you.

54
00:03:27.066 --> 00:03:30.900
She's the daughter of a highly regarded family in Fleurrh City.

55
00:03:30.966 --> 00:03:34.366
She's exceptional at all things performance-related.

56
00:03:34.433 --> 00:03:36.866
We'd be honored if you'd be her mentor.

57
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.466
I will only judge what I see with my very own eyes.

58
00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:42.533
Oh.

59
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.300
Oh, yes, of course.

60
00:03:45.366 --> 00:03:49.900
I'm sure when you get to see Amelia's performance, you'll be quite pleased.

61
00:03:54.966 --> 00:03:58.433
Bonjour, Pokémon lovers, and welcome.

62
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.400
Get ready for a competition magnifique.

63
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.266
The Fleurrh City Pokémon Showcase will delight

64
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:07.166
as we present our Rookie Class Division.

65
00:04:10.766 --> 00:04:13.300
Alors, I'm your dreamworld guide,

66
00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.033
Monsieur Pierre.

67
00:04:15.633 --> 00:04:19.700
Tonight's winner will be one step closer to becoming Kalos Queen.

68
00:04:20.266 --> 00:04:22.700
What will she win?

69
00:04:22.766 --> 00:04:25.200
This beautiful Princess Key.

70
00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.066
- Serena?
- Huh?

71
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.666
Kiri and Kazalie, please get ready.

72
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.233
Right.

73
00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:40.166
The Theme Performance for today's Pokémon Showcase is...

74
00:04:56.633 --> 00:04:57.533
Rhyhorn?

75
00:04:58.066 --> 00:05:02.233
Oh, wow. Look at all those Rhyhorn. So cute.

76
00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.600
A Rhyhorn performance? Whoa.

77
00:05:04.666 --> 00:05:06.000
Pika?

78
00:05:06.066 --> 00:05:09.933
Alors, the Kalos Queen must possess the power

79
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.066
to attract the heart of a Pokémon.

80
00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:17.333
So, the performer who attracts the most Rhyhorn within the time limit

81
00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.900
will move on to the Freestyle Performance.

82
00:05:19.966 --> 00:05:22.633
And it doesn't matter how they accomplish it.

83
00:05:23.466 --> 00:05:25.333
Hey, this is perfect.

84
00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.700
Yeah. Serena's great at this.

85
00:05:27.766 --> 00:05:32.500
But no one ever knows what will happen. She's gotta stay sharp the whole time.

86
00:05:32.566 --> 00:05:36.500
Now for the first group of performers. Here they are.

87
00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.500
Serena!

88
00:05:43.566 --> 00:05:45.100
She's in the first group.

89
00:05:45.166 --> 00:05:46.600
You can do it, Serena!

90
00:05:46.666 --> 00:05:47.800
- Pika!
- Chespin!

91
00:05:47.866 --> 00:05:48.733
Bunnelby!

92
00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.233
Maintenant, let's begin.

93
00:05:55.733 --> 00:05:56.833
- All right.
- Scrag!

94
00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:57.933
Okay, come here.

95
00:05:58.833 --> 00:06:01.600
- Lilligant, let's surround them.
- Lilli.

96
00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.266
- Cham.
- Braixen.

97
00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.966
Rhyhorn.

98
00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:15.933
- Now, everybody stay calm, okay?
- Pancham.

99
00:06:18.766 --> 00:06:22.833
Whoa. The Rhyhorn are all heading to Serena.

100
00:06:23.466 --> 00:06:24.566
I knew it.

101
00:06:24.633 --> 00:06:25.700
I knew it, too.

102
00:06:25.766 --> 00:06:27.433
Hey, wait! Hold on!

103
00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.766
Of course, those Rhyhorn really like Serena.

104
00:06:33.833 --> 00:06:36.666
No fair. I wanna be cuddled, too.

105
00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:38.600
Braix.

106
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.966
Stop it. Cut it out. Huh?

107
00:06:49.766 --> 00:06:53.366
- Huh?
- Lilligant, use sweet scent.

108
00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.833
Good Rhyhorn, over here.

109
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.400
Kazalie is attracting the Rhyhorn with sweet scent.

110
00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:07.666
- Didn't think of that.
- Only a short time left.

111
00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.733
Sorry. Let me through.

112
00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:15.233
You were startled, weren't you?

113
00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.733
Everything's all right.

114
00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.033
- Rhy.
- Huh?

115
00:07:18.966 --> 00:07:23.333
I know. The Rhyhorn back home like it when I scratch them right here.

116
00:07:23.966 --> 00:07:25.133
Rhy.

117
00:07:32.233 --> 00:07:35.500
- Okay, now. Nice and slow.
- Rhy!

118
00:07:40.366 --> 00:07:41.366
Time is up.

119
00:07:43.433 --> 00:07:46.800
Alors, the performer with the most Rhyhorn is...

120
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.766
- Performer Serena!
- Ah!

121
00:07:50.333 --> 00:07:52.333
Oh!

122
00:07:53.466 --> 00:07:55.166
- All right!
- Pika!

123
00:07:55.233 --> 00:07:56.966
- Go, Serena!
- I knew it.

124
00:08:05.733 --> 00:08:09.366
Here is our final group for the Theme Performance.

125
00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.766
Amelia!

126
00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.666
That performer has the hometown advantage,

127
00:08:16.733 --> 00:08:19.366
so, it might not be that easy a win for Serena.

128
00:08:19.433 --> 00:08:20.266
Huh?

129
00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:21.900
Begin.

130
00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:25.100
Espeon, Dragonair, attract, let's go.

131
00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:32.633
Now, everyone, come over here.

132
00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.400
And the final performer to move on

133
00:08:43.466 --> 00:08:46.666
to the Freestyle Performance is Amelia.

134
00:08:50.233 --> 00:08:51.833
Ladies and gentlemen...

135
00:08:52.266 --> 00:08:56.166
Ladies and gentlemen, we now begin the Freestyle Performance,

136
00:08:56.233 --> 00:08:59.633
lovingly choreographed by our performers themselves.

137
00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.566
You, the audience, will be our judges.

138
00:09:02.633 --> 00:09:04.900
Once all performances have concluded,

139
00:09:04.966 --> 00:09:07.866
cast your vote by lighting your Glow Casters

140
00:09:07.933 --> 00:09:11.333
with the color of the performer you think did best.

141
00:09:11.766 --> 00:09:14.700
Alors, here is our first performer.

142
00:09:17.466 --> 00:09:20.366
There. You're all set and ready to go.

143
00:09:20.433 --> 00:09:21.566
Braixen, Brai.

144
00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:28.800
Vee.

145
00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.133
Hmm.

146
00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.333
Don't forget,

147
00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:40.100
we practiced really hard for this.

148
00:09:40.166 --> 00:09:41.900
- Sylveon.
- Huh?

149
00:09:44.366 --> 00:09:45.266
I've got it.

150
00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.400
Have a Poké Puff.

151
00:09:48.833 --> 00:09:51.500
Ash said eating will give you lots of energy.

152
00:09:52.666 --> 00:09:54.266
Of course you can have one.

153
00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:55.833
Braixen, Braixen.

154
00:09:58.400 --> 00:09:59.266
Braix.

155
00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:02.966
-And this one's just for you.

156
00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:04.900
Eon.

157
00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:10.500
- Sylvee.
- Sylveon, it's okay if we're not perfect.

158
00:10:10.566 --> 00:10:12.566
So, let's just dance and have fun.

159
00:10:13.033 --> 00:10:14.600
You dance wonderfully.

160
00:10:14.666 --> 00:10:15.966
Let's go show them.

161
00:10:17.266 --> 00:10:18.333
Eon.

162
00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:21.366
Let's have a great time out onstage.

163
00:10:21.433 --> 00:10:22.800
- Eon.
- Braixen.

164
00:10:22.866 --> 00:10:23.700
Pancham.

165
00:10:24.533 --> 00:10:27.500
And now it's time for our next performer.

166
00:10:27.566 --> 00:10:28.566
Amelia!

167
00:10:31.033 --> 00:10:33.000
Who's that Pokémon?

168
00:10:38.666 --> 00:10:41.000
It's Espeon.

169
00:10:41.066 --> 00:10:43.966
Eon!

170
00:10:47.233 --> 00:10:48.133
Go!

171
00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.200
All right, Espeon, use psychic.

172
00:10:54.266 --> 00:10:56.433
Dragonair, dragon dance.

173
00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.833
Espeon!

174
00:11:07.966 --> 00:11:11.000
Espeon and Dragonair, use attract.

175
00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:22.666
Espeon, rain dance.

176
00:11:22.733 --> 00:11:24.200
Espee.

177
00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.966
Now, Dragonair, use ice beam.

178
00:11:37.066 --> 00:11:38.366
Hyper voice.

179
00:11:39.933 --> 00:11:42.166
Espee!

180
00:11:46.433 --> 00:11:47.266
Finished.

181
00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:50.200
Beautiful.

182
00:11:50.566 --> 00:11:53.800
Just what you'd expect from one of the top contenders.

183
00:11:56.533 --> 00:11:59.966
Uh-oh. I think that attract is working on Chespin.

184
00:12:02.133 --> 00:12:05.933
- Next up, it's Serena!
- Ah.

185
00:12:06.966 --> 00:12:08.700
- There she is.
- Pika!

186
00:12:08.766 --> 00:12:09.766
Hi, Serena.

187
00:12:09.833 --> 00:12:11.633
Just relax. Just relax.

188
00:12:16.133 --> 00:12:17.933
Braixen, flamethrower.

189
00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.866
- Fairy wind, go.
- Yon.

190
00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.533
Pancham, you're up.

191
00:12:41.933 --> 00:12:44.800
- Pancham!
- Yon!

192
00:12:44.866 --> 00:12:46.100
Cham!

193
00:12:52.933 --> 00:12:55.266
- Serena's doing great.
- Pika!

194
00:13:21.866 --> 00:13:24.700
- It's amazing.
- Looks like they're having fun.

195
00:13:24.766 --> 00:13:27.633
You bet. It's a lot of fun watching them, too.

196
00:13:29.433 --> 00:13:30.466
Hmm.

197
00:13:31.433 --> 00:13:33.366
Now let's wrap it up.

198
00:13:42.366 --> 00:13:45.466
- Braixen!
- Eon!

199
00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:54.833
Tada!

200
00:14:02.266 --> 00:14:04.333
Wasn't that lots of fun?

201
00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:12.400
Alors, who will be our beautiful and elegant winner?

202
00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:16.133
Light your Glow Casters with the color that corresponds

203
00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.166
to the performer who you think was the best.

204
00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.366
We have the results.

205
00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:48.566
The Fleurrh City Pokémon Showcase winner...

206
00:14:51.633 --> 00:14:53.666
is Serena!

207
00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:56.733
All right!

208
00:14:57.466 --> 00:14:58.333
Awesome.

209
00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:01.833
She did it!

210
00:15:04.833 --> 00:15:05.800
Hmm.

211
00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.233
And as promised,

212
00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:14.100
our winner will now receive this elegant and beautiful Princess Key.

213
00:15:14.166 --> 00:15:16.066
- Klefki!
- Tada!

214
00:15:16.133 --> 00:15:20.300
I just received my third Princess Key, and we did it together.

215
00:15:22.133 --> 00:15:25.633
Congratulations on winning your third Princess Key.

216
00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:29.566
You now have the opportunity to compete in the Master Class.

217
00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.866
It's true.

218
00:15:31.533 --> 00:15:32.700
It's happening.

219
00:15:34.666 --> 00:15:36.933
- Braixen!
- Pancham!

220
00:15:48.366 --> 00:15:50.000
Tada! Yeah!

221
00:15:50.066 --> 00:15:52.000
Congratulations, Serena.

222
00:15:52.066 --> 00:15:54.300
Thanks. It's like a dream.

223
00:15:54.366 --> 00:15:57.300
I'm going to stand on the same stage as Aria.

224
00:15:57.366 --> 00:16:01.300
Not a dream. You're going to compete against her as a performer.

225
00:16:01.366 --> 00:16:03.533
I really am, aren't I?

226
00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:04.533
That's right.

227
00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.033
And me, too.

228
00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:10.466
That's why I'm practicing really, really hard for my Master Class performance.

229
00:16:10.533 --> 00:16:12.433
Huh? Hmm.

230
00:16:12.866 --> 00:16:14.733
Well, I'm not going to lose.

231
00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.666
- Okay, Serena, we're ready for you.
- Huh?

232
00:16:17.733 --> 00:16:19.900
- Shauna, I have to go.
- Okay.

233
00:16:19.966 --> 00:16:22.500
Hurry, hurry! It's important!

234
00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:25.833
What's the rush? We don't have to hurry.

235
00:16:27.933 --> 00:16:29.766
We're celebrating your chance

236
00:16:29.833 --> 00:16:32.300
- to compete in the Master Class.
- Amazing.

237
00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:38.333
- You made all this food?
- Yes, there's plenty, so eat all you want.

238
00:16:39.166 --> 00:16:42.600
I made special food for Braixen and the other Pokémon.

239
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.333
There's more than enough for everyone.

240
00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.633
- Yeah!
- Yay!

241
00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:51.333
- Pika, Pika.
- Chespin, Che.

242
00:16:57.433 --> 00:16:58.266
Huh?

243
00:17:03.766 --> 00:17:05.366
Pika.

244
00:17:08.666 --> 00:17:11.300
Braixen? Pancham? Sylveon?

245
00:17:12.166 --> 00:17:13.833
It's time for a good brushing.

246
00:17:15.633 --> 00:17:16.533
Huh?

247
00:17:23.333 --> 00:17:25.566
So, is this what you're looking for?

248
00:17:25.633 --> 00:17:26.633
Yes.

249
00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:28.200
Thank you so very much.

250
00:17:28.266 --> 00:17:29.433
You're welcome.

251
00:17:31.133 --> 00:17:33.600
Now let's go back so I can brush you.

252
00:17:33.666 --> 00:17:35.700
- Yon.
- Pancham.

253
00:17:36.533 --> 00:17:37.633
Hold on.

254
00:17:38.066 --> 00:17:39.466
This is unacceptable.

255
00:17:41.866 --> 00:17:45.266
Mine was a much more polished performance than hers was.

256
00:17:46.533 --> 00:17:47.366
Is that...?

257
00:17:47.433 --> 00:17:48.966
- Cham.
- Braixen.

258
00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.800
Yet the fact remains you lost. That's simply how the audience judged it.

259
00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:59.700
Isn't there something more productive you could be doing?

260
00:17:59.766 --> 00:18:02.900
But I want to become a better performer than Aria.

261
00:18:06.266 --> 00:18:08.700
You can't just win with a perfect score.

262
00:18:09.433 --> 00:18:13.300
The only person who can come up with something more than that is you.

263
00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.800
- Young lady?
- Huh?

264
